// GPU marching-cubes mesher for one terrain chunk.
//
// Mirrors the CPU mesher in src/engine/services/Terrain.odin:
//   * terrain_march_cell / MC_March_Cube_Edges  -> the cube pass
//   * terrain_edge_vertex (one vertex per lattice edge) -> the edge pass
//   * terrain_normal_at_world / terrain_sample_occupancy -> normalAt()
//   * terrain_material_weights_at_world -> materialWeightsAt()
//
// Two passes over the same storage buffers, dispatched back to back with a
// compute->compute barrier between them:
//
//   pass 1 (edge pass): one thread per lattice edge in the chunk's 17^3 corner
//     lattice. A cut edge (its two corner occupancies straddle the iso level)
//     allocates one output vertex and records its index in edge_vert; the
//     vertex's normal and material weights are computed here, exactly once per
//     edge, so shared vertices are not recomputed.
//
//   pass 2 (cube pass): one thread per 16^3 cell. Reads MC_TRI to find each
//     cell's triangles, maps their cube-local edges to the shared edge_vert
//     indices written by pass 1, orients each face to the outward normal, and
//     appends the triangle to the index buffer.
//
// The direct-mapped edge_vert array (no hashing) is what makes this race-free:
// an edge's slot is unique, so pass 1 never writes the same index twice and
// pass 2 only ever reads indices that are already final.
//
// NOTE: This is a template; the table marker below is replaced by
// tools/gen_terrain_mc_tables.py, which writes the finished kine_terrain_mc.comp
// compiled by the build. Edit this file, not the generated one.

